          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "પત્રકાર — patrakār — \"a journalist\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "એક પત્રકારે મીરાને ઘણા પ્રશ્ન પૂછ્યા. ek patrakāre Mīrāne ghaṇā praśna pūchyā. A journalist asked Mira a lot of questions."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine or feminine noun, by the person meant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "પત્રકાર (patrakār) is built from પત્ર, a letter or a printed sheet, from Sanskrit patra, \"a leaf\", and -kār, \"a maker\" (Monier-Williams): the one who makes the paper. It is used of a man or a woman."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
